          now fulfilment through the online store). Answers that commit only
          to "product" can still score if the reasoning is precise about why
          the service element is secondary.
        explain_expected: |
          A product is a tangible good transferred to the customer. A service
          is an action or experience provided to the customer. The bookshop
          transfers physical books (product) but also offers curation, staff
          expertise, and fulfilment logistics (service). The online store
          extends the service dimension because it introduces delivery,
          account management, and digital browsing.
