          Classifying the business as product-plus-service drives which
          digital tools the owner should prioritise: a simple product
          catalogue and payment system is not enough. She also needs
          inventory synchronisation between the shop and the website,
          customer accounts, delivery management, and ideally recommendation
          features that preserve the curation experience online.
      exemplar_answer: |
        The bookshop provides both a product and a service. The product is
        the physical books themselves, which transfer ownership to the
        customer when purchased. The service is the curation, recommendations,
        and fulfilment experience that wraps around those books, and which
        the online store will need to replicate digitally through features
        like a searchable catalogue, customer accounts, and delivery
        tracking. Treating the business as product-only would lead the
        owner to buy only a basic e-commerce platform, missing the tools
        that preserve what makes her shop distinctive and losing the
        customer loyalty that a small independent depends on.
